ist","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.rfrrealestate.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Buy, Sell or Lease","item":"https://www.rfrrealestate.com/buy-sell-lease"}]}]},
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How buying works in Ras Al Khaimah","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Brief and shortlist","text":"Budget, purpose and timing. We shortlist ready homes and launches worth your time, and say which to skip."},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Viewings and checks","text":"In person, or on video from abroad. We check the developer, the service charge and the title before you commit."},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Offer and paperwork","text":"We negotiate the price or the payment plan, then the sale agreement and the developer's no-objection certificate."},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Transfer and keys","text":"Registration with the RAK Land Department, then handover. The same advisor stays with you afterwards."}]},
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can foreigners buy property in Ras Al Khaimah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, in the designated freehold areas. Ras Al Khaimah Municipality lists them as Al Hamra Village, Mina Al Arab, Al Marjan Island, RAK Central, Julphar Towers, Al Maareedh (plots) and the upcoming Beach District. UAE and GCC nationals can buy anywhere in the Emirate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does buying property in Ras Al Khaimah give me a Golden Visa?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can. Property worth AED 2M or more can qualify you for a UAE Golden Visa, subject to the federal ICP rules at the time you apply. Official pages differ on whether the property route gives 5 or 10 years, so confirm the term with ICP or your RAK channel. RFR does not issue visas or give immigration advice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What government fees do I pay when buying in Ras Al Khaimah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The buyer pays a registration fee of 2% of the market value to RAK Municipality, plus AED 200 for plan issuance and AED 200 for the title deed. If you use a mortgage, its registration costs 0.1% of the loan. Agency commission and developer charges are separate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to be in the UAE to buy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not necessarily. We run viewings over video for buyers abroad, a power of attorney can be used if someone acts for you at the transfer, and we can manage the property once you own it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there tax on property in the UAE?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There is no income tax or capital gains tax on property in the UAE. The registration fees still apply when you buy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s the difference between buying off-plan and buying a ready home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Off-plan means paying in instalments for a home that isn’t finished yet, usually at a lower entry price. A ready home costs more upfront but you can view and move into it straight away."}}]}
